# SLAAPS wind-tunnel profile A: fixed gains modeled at 20 m/s, schedule OFF. Written 2026-11-19. NOTHING HERE IS MEASURED.
# Load AFTER slaaps_vehicle.params and slaaps_canard_trims.params. Apply with SLA_CFG_APPLY +1 while disarmed.
# Same method as data revision 3 (see docs/SLAAPS_DATA_RECORD.md, revision 4): every canard derivative, the moment scales and
# SLA_AIRSPD / SLA_Cn_WASH are declared at ONE airflow, 20 m/s. The derivatives and SLA_x_M_SCALE / SP_ACC are the revision-3 (40 m/s)
# values x (20/40)^2 = 0.25; RATE_P and RATE_I are divided by 0.25 (x4), so the loop crossover is unchanged: about 5 rad/s roll and
# 4 rad/s pitch and yaw at 20 m/s, falling with V^2 at lower speed and rising above it. ATT_P and the stick rates are unchanged.
# Use ONLY when the true flow at the vehicle is about 20 m/s. At 40 m/s these gains are about 4x too aggressive; at 13 m/s about 2.4x too weak.
# The pitot must read the true speed (positive, tracking the tunnel reference) before you rely on it.
# This file sets SLA_DATA_REV 4 and SLA_DATA_STATE 0: the lead must declare it before Manual can arm (SLA_DATA_STATE 1).
1	1	SLA_SCH_EN	0	6
1	1	SLA_DATA_REV	4	6
1	1	SLA_DATA_STATE	0	6
1	1	SLA_AIRSPD	20	9
